*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
docs/notes/
CHANGELOG_data_model.md

# Use-case graphs covered by an NDA. These stay on disk for local assessment
# runs but must never enter the repository. Nothing in the test suite or the
# shipped library depends on them: the project's own example graphs live in
# ontology/example/ and are tracked normally.
docs/example_UC/

# Your own architecture graphs. Drop anything here - confidential, NDA-covered,
# half-finished - and the workbench will offer it in Load example when you run
# it locally, while git ignores every file in the folder and the Docker build
# leaves the folder out of the image entirely. Only the README is tracked, so
# the folder still exists in a fresh clone to say what it is for.
# test_local_examples.py fails if anything else here ever becomes tracked.
ontology/example_local/*
!ontology/example_local/README.md


outputs/*.ttl
outputs/output_*/
data/processed/**
!data/processed/
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/processed/outputs/
!data/processed/outputs/.gitkeep
